# Line endings, decided here rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# Development happens on Windows and deployment is a `git pull` on Linux, which
# is exactly the arrangement where a CRLF slips into a file that cannot survive
# one. A shell script with CRLF fails on its shebang -- `/usr/bin/env bash\r:
# no such file or directory` -- and a systemd unit with CRLF is rejected as
# malformed. Neither failure names its cause.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf

# PowerShell runs only on Windows, where CRLF is native.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Never touched, never diffed as text.
*.pdf       binary
